3.2 Tsarin amincewa da bank destination
Admin mai izini ya shigar da bayanan asusu a matsayin draft.
Ya aiko config don dubawa (pending_approval).
Authorized verifier ya tabbatar da bank/provider account ta hanyar da kamfani ya amince da ita, tare da rubuta source da date. Screenshot na bank details shi kaɗai ba ya maye gurbin independent verification.
A fi so maker-checker: mutumin da ya ƙirƙiri/gyara bank destination kada shi kaɗai ya kunna shi. Mai duba na biyu ya amince da bayanan asusu da verification.
Sai bayan verification_status = verified da approval ne config zai iya zama active.
Canza account number, account name, bank/provider ko currency yana ƙirƙirar sabon config version, kuma yana buƙatar sake verification/approval. Kada a gyara active version a baya.
A ƙyale active destination guda ɗaya ga Mainnet + NGN a kowane lokaci, sai dai product owner ya amince da multi-account design daga baya.
Idan babu verified active bank config, API ta dawo da bank_transfer_available: false; UI ya ɓoye ko disable bank transfer, amma Pi payment na iya kasancewa dabam idan an kunna shi kuma an tabbatar da policy.
3.3 “Enable” ba yana nufin “verified” ba
A ware abubuwa biyu:
verification_status: ko an tabbatar da destination.
enabled: ko product owner ya ba da izinin karɓar bank transfer a wannan environment.
enabled = true kaɗai bai isa ba. API ta duba duka verified state, approval state, active version, currency, effective dates da environment kafin ta nuna hanyar biya.
4. Bank transfer workflow
4.1 Mai amfani
Ya shiga ta shared Pi authentication.
Ya zaɓi service type kuma ya karɓi quote mai quote_id, amount, currency, valid-until da terms version.
Backend ya ƙirƙiri dapp_service_request da payment_intent da ke nuni da quote.
Idan bank transfer yana available, backend ya ba UI bank details daga verified active config; UI zai nuna amount, currency, account details, payment reference da expiration.
Mai amfani ya aika transfer daga bank app dinsa.
Ya shigar da transaction reference da ranar/amount da aka tura; receipt upload na iya zama optional evidence bisa policy.
Intent ya shiga submitted_for_review; payment remains pending_verification.
Mai amfani zai ga status da admin-facing next step. Kada UI ya ce “Paid/Confirmed” har sai backend ya tabbatar.
4.2 Admin reconciliation
Admin mai izini ya duba:
actual credit/transaction a official bank portal/statement ko wata source da kamfani ya amince da ita;
account/beneficiary da ya karɓi kuɗi;
amount da currency da aka sa a quote;
transaction date/time;
reference/provider identifier;
matching service request/payment intent;
yiwuwar duplicate reference ko reused evidence.
Sakamakon da Admin zai zaɓa:
confirmed — kawai idan actual credit ya bayyana kuma duk checks sun dace;
rejected — idan an tabbatar cewa payment ƙarya ne ko bai dace ba, tare da reason;
needs_more_evidence — idan bayanai ba su isa ba;
ya bar pending_verification idan ba a iya tantancewa ba tukuna.
A rubuta actor, time, decision, reason, evidence source type, old/new status da config version a audit trail. Kada a adana cikakken bank statement ko bayanan da ba su da alaƙa fiye da abin da policy ta buƙata.
4.3 Dokokin anti-duplication
Normalize transaction reference (trim/normalize case inda ya dace) kafin comparison.
Ƙirƙiri unique/guard rule na reference bisa destination/config/provider. Idan bank provider bai ba da unique global reference ba, a ayyana composite matching rule; kada a ƙirƙiri unique constraint na ƙarya da zai hana legitimate payment.
Intent ɗaya ba zai iya haifar da confirmed event fiye da ɗaya ba.
Reference/evidence ɗaya ba za a iya yi wa intents daban-daban confirmed ba ba tare da explicit exception workflow da audit ba.
Admin double-click, API retry da concurrent review su kasance idempotent/transactional.
5. Payment status da request status
Payment intent status
created → pending_payment → submitted_for_review → confirmed
Sauran halayen da za su iya faruwa: rejected, failed, cancelled, expired, refund_pending, refunded. Aiwatar da refund states ne kawai bayan refund policy da izini sun samu amincewa.
Bank transfer verification status (idan ana son field daban)
not_submitted, pending_verification, needs_more_evidence, confirmed, rejected.
Request/service delivery status
draft → submitted → under_review → approved / revision_requested / rejected → in_progress → completed.
Kada a haɗa waɗannan a field ɗaya. Payment confirmed ba ya nuna cewa request approved ne ko aikin dApp ya kammala; request approved kuma ba ya tabbatar da biyan kuɗi.
6. Database contract — proposed objects only
Sunaye na ƙasa shawarwari ne, za a daidaita su da naming convention da schema mai rai kafin migration.
6.1 dapp_service_payment_configs
Purpose: versioned bank destination/settings and payment availability.
Proposed fields:
id uuid primary key
network text not null (mainnet or testnet)
payment_method text not null (bank_transfer; Pi method configuration may live here or a distinct table)
version integer not null
display_name text, bank_name text, account_name text, account_number text, currency text
payment_instructions text
verification_status text not null
config_status text not null
enabled boolean not null default false
verification_source_type text, verification_note text
verified_by uuid, verified_at timestamptz
created_by uuid, created_at timestamptz, updated_at timestamptz
approved_by uuid, approved_at timestamptz, effective_from timestamptz, retired_at timestamptz
Constraints / handling:
Validate status transitions server-side/RPC.
One active destination per network + payment method + currency, unless later approved otherwise.
No anonymous/browser insert or update.
Direct public table access is not required; expose only safe active details from an API/RPC view with least privilege.
If account details are treated as operational configuration rather than secret credentials, they still require write access controls and audit; do not expose draft/retired versions to payers.
6.2 Existing/new dapp_service_requests
Request ownership derives from trusted server-validated Pi identity, not a client-supplied UID.
network and service/request status are server-enforced.
Avoid making user identity editable after creation.
6.3 dapp_service_quotes
id, request_id, service type, price revision, amount, currency, optional pi_amount, pi_currency only if policy defines them, terms version, created/valid-until, quote status, created by/source.
Quote amount and currency are server-owned. Frontend cannot override them.
Quote acceptance stores accepted quote ID/version/time; expired quotes cannot create new intents.
6.4 dapp_service_payment_intents
id, request_id, quote_id, network, method, amount, currency, status, client_reference or server-generated reference, config_id, config_version, destination_snapshot (safe immutable snapshot), provider_payment_id for Pi flow where applicable, idempotency key/hash, expiry and timestamps.
destination_snapshot records the exact verified pay-to destination shown when intent was created. It must not change if Admin rotates bank configuration later.
Prevent one provider payment ID from being attached to multiple intents within the same relevant network/provider scope.
Store only safe display destination fields in snapshot; never store bank login credentials, PIN or OTP.
6.5 dapp_service_payment_evidence
Intent ID, evidence type, private storage object path, uploaded by, content type verified server-side, byte size, hash, created at, review state.
Avoid storing public URLs. Only authorized backend/admin can issue a time-limited download link.
6.6 dapp_service_payment_events
Append-only event stream: event ID, intent ID, network, old/new state, actor type/ID, source, reason code, short safe note, provider reference, created at, request correlation ID.
Prefer blocking direct update/delete for browser roles. Audit rows should not be editable by normal Admin UI.
6.7 Migration discipline
Do not run SQL directly in production from this design doc.
Before writing migration, re-introspect Mainnet + Testnet schema, grants, RLS policies, role/AAL2 checks and existing audit conventions.
Test migration on isolated Testnet/staging first, including negative tests for anon, authenticated, unauthorized Admin, Admin without AAL2, cross-network access and direct table mutation.
