8. Pi payment contract — remains separate
Pi payment uses the official Pi SDK and documented server-side payment handshake for the registered app.
Backend validates the user's Pi access token through the documented Pi identity endpoint, and retrieves payment data from Pi Platform API as appropriate.
Backend matches the Pi payment to a server-created dApp-service intent and compares expected amount, metadata, UID ownership, network and status before approval/completion.
Use a dApp-specific action/memo/metadata namespace; do not loosen or override existing investment/liquidity metadata validation, especially add_liquidity checks.
Never trust browser amount, callback success, transaction ID, request ID or metadata without independent server verification.
Approval and completion retries must be idempotent; incomplete payments need a recovery/reconciliation path.
Record provider payment ID and confirmed transaction identifier; only server confirmation can set payment_status = confirmed.
Do not invent or freeze endpoint/request details until the currently published Pi Developer Documentation and exact SDK version used in ALBUKHR are rechecked immediately before coding.
